PYTHON LEVEL 4 — FINAL INTERVIEW CHEAT SHEET (PRECISE)

Memorize this as-is.

1️⃣ GIL (Global Interpreter Lock)

“The GIL is a mutex in CPython that allows only one thread to execute Python bytecode at a time, simplifying memory management but limiting CPU-bound multithreading.”

2️⃣ GIL Impact

“The GIL affects CPU-bound tasks but not I/O-bound tasks.”

3️⃣ Multithreading

“Multithreading uses multiple threads within the same process but is limited by the GIL for CPU-bound tasks in CPython.”

4️⃣ Multiprocessing

“Multiprocessing uses multiple processes with separate memory spaces, bypassing the GIL and enabling true parallelism.”

5️⃣ CPU-bound vs I/O-bound

“CPU-bound tasks require heavy computation, while I/O-bound tasks spend most of their time waiting for external resources.”

6️⃣ Async Programming

“Async programming enables concurrent execution of I/O-bound tasks using a single thread and an event loop.”

7️⃣ Event Loop

“An event loop schedules and switches between asynchronous tasks when they are waiting for I/O.”

8️⃣ Async Limitation

“Async programming is not suitable for CPU-bound tasks.”
